> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1365223-can-you-play-a-\u201cgood\u201d-ghast#post1365223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are my most favorite Thallain kith. It also seems like one that could use their Birthright for good, as like a actual surgeon lTheir frailty is pretty bad, but you can survive with only one Kidney.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run Kinain where you can have Birthrights. A Kinain of a Ghast could be tussling with their darkside ala Dexter and or being entirely good and striving to use the power given to them by their horrible ancestor to make ammends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T19:54:38-07:00","id":1390443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1365223-can-you-play-a-\u201cgood\u201d-ghast?p=1365411#post1365411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're children of the Fomorians, so it's not really possible. <i>Maybe</i> if the Ghast is half-Tuathan, if such a thing is even possible. That doesn't seem to make a difference with any of the half-Fomorians running about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I respectfully disagree... Difficult, indeed, but possible...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T06:06:12-07:00","id":1390964,"title":"","content":"Yeah I can see the idea of forcing Thallain to take Oaths as a possible solution to kind of half rehabilitate them. And if you allow it even take oaths of Fealty to Houses.<br /> <br /> Some of my Designs, like with my Project for Yokai, have Homebrew Gallain that incorporate Thallain. Like a type of Gallain centered around the Family of Lilith include Thallain among their Numbers. And the Kami of Heaven, Earth and Hell including Thallain or Yokai with some Nightmare Legacies as part of the Tribes/Clans of Oni for the Yomi no Kami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T21:48:49-07:00","id":1393741,"title":"","content":"If an Unseelie can hang around Thallain enough to &quot;catch&quot; their &quot;cousin's&quot; Thallain Birthright or Frailty; then a Thallain might be able to do the reverse. That might give the Thallain a nascent conscience and trade a Nightmare Legacy for an Arcadian one. Going by the sidhe Thallain writeup -- they'd likely be permanently Unseelie. but at least they wouldn't be <i>Thallain</i>...<br /> <br /> You'd have to hide that from the rest of the Black Court and it rarely ends well. Maybe they'd reincarnate as Kithain in their next life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","user":"Saint Michael","date":". 06-03-2020, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}